"P0" ""

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - ScottNeuronMoralChoiceClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2873710796" "Fall of the Olympian"
// DetailString :
"P1414453869" "Calvin Scott wants you to destroy every line of data and every scrap of physical material surrounding The Olympian. The project is too dangerous to be allowed to exist in the hands of Tyrant and his supporters."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef - NeuronMoralChoice 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef Name :
"P3237182257" "The Sleeping Emperor"
// tDetailString :
"P3234101336" "You remember walking into Neuron's lab and there, floating in a stasis tube, was the spitting image of the Emperor, Marcus Cole. But you knew that it was not him. It was a being called The Olympian, a genetic copy of Marcus Cole created by Neuron. That he looked identical to the Emperor was not a coincidence, it merely showed that Neuron's belief was to take: <br><br><color gold>Pride in Your Work</color><br><br>After defeating The Olympian on the steps of the Magisterium, Neuron was in a panic. He knew that Emperor Cole would be very displeased in the rather public failure of Neuron's latest test, and that sentiment was an understatement. The political spin doctors had already been announcing that what had transpired was actually a Resistance plot that you had thankfully uncovered, but the Emperor's displeasure was still great. He ordered Neuron to halt The Olympian program and destroy the subject.<br><br>Neuron disagreed with the decision and proclaimed, to you and you alone, that he would do no such thing. Such was his pride in his work that he could not see that what he did completely undermined the Emperor's authority. He sent you in to destroy The Olympian as he was instructed, but had no intention of destroying his research data.<br><br>What Neuron didn't realize is that, like him, you also take pride in your work."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Scott 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P63363795" "{HeroName}, good job in taking down The Olympian. Cole is working the PR angle directly, explaning to the public that it was a Resistance ploy that due to your quick action stopped before it got out of hand.<br><br>What's the real story here?"
// Answer Text :
"P2628720815" "Neuron was making mass produced super powered soldiers."
// Page InformationPage1 Text :
"P1878491760" "Mass produced? We could barely hold off one of them and he's planning on making an army of these things?"
// Answer Text :
"P2569026877" "Cole ordered him to halt production for now."
// Page InformationPage2 Text :
"P4030776964" "I see, Neuron hit too close to the mark then. What seems to be the situation now, though?"
// Answer Text :
"P3348459781" "Neuron is going to continue work on it in secret."
// Page InformationPage3 Text :
"P684866648" "We can't allow that to happen. Neuron will continue work on The Olympian either with or without Cole's permission, and even if the emperor discovers this there is no doubt in my mind that what research Neuron has already done will be used against us somehow.<br><br>I want you to destroy every scrap of data and physical material surrounding that project. The Olympian and every advancement achieved in his production needs to be destroyed."
// Answer Text :
"P4262229902" "Understood."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - ColeTree 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P3334935145" "Considering recent events I assume that your message is of significance."
// Answer Text :
"P2098022539" "It is, my lord."
// Page InformationPage1 Text :
"P1008390790" "Please, you are one of Praetoria's greatest defenders, you have both my respect and my admiration. Dispense with the titles and call me Marcus."
// Answer Text :
"P335689459" "Marcus, Praetor Berry has chosen not to follow your orders."
// Page Page2 Text :
"P1853849753" "I see. Stephen Berry has ever been difficult to control. It is, unfortunately, one of his many and varied flaws. That you suggest we must now add disloyalty is concerning to me. Do you have proof of this?"
// Answer Text :
"P3251386811" "The Olympian will be destroyed, but the data will not."
// Page Page3 Text :
"P2647727986" "I see, and I can understand his desire to keep his research, but there are two reasons why I stand by my decision. First, I believe The Olympian project was too dangerous. It was powerful but was uncontrollable.<br><br>Second, I gave Neuron a direct order based on what I had observed. That he chooses to ignore the latter despite the former is greatly concerning. It tells me he has grown blind with pride."
// Answer Text :
"P916303965" "Marcus, if you wish, I will carry out your order."
// Page ChoiceA Text :
"P634088383" "It is not a matter of me wishing, {HeroName}, but rather of me hoping. That you would do the right thing is of great comfort to me. I shall deal with Stephen and The Olympian.<br><br>I shall have to remind Praetor Berry that he should not grow too prideful. Too many have already forgotten how hubris nearly destroyed us all."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P1249365534" "Cole has informed me that my project is to be canceled immediately. He has no idea what he is throwing away here! We're so close to success, I just need a little time to figure out exactly what went wrong. I'm sure it's something to do with the Limbo Device, but I don't know exactly what."
// AcceptString :
"P346499537" "Ask what he's going to do."
// SendOffString :
"P1888306575" "Cole only need know that the current version of The Olympian is destroyed, but my research will continue. When I have finally overcome whatever critical flaw I overlooked, then Cole will realize that I did the right thing.<br><br>Go in and disconnect that flawed chunk of flesh from the nutrient vat. It is of no use to me any more."
// ActiveTaskString :
"P1491336560" "Disconnect The Olympian (Single Player)"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P3589301195" "Cole has requested that The Olympian be destroyed immediately. The hubris of that man believing that he knows better than I when science is concerned!"
// TaskTitle :
"P1639457485" "<color deepskyblue>Pride in Your Work</color>"
// TaskSubTitle :
"P1941949693" "<color deepskyblue>Finale: Following Orders</color>"

